  tierReadouts:
  - TierLabel: LV1 Escort Probe
    StageRole: Low-cost boss proxy that holds the lane long enough for the player
      to answer with fire or a saved summon.
    PlayerRead: Strafe and keep firing; spend SummonSlot1 only if the next barrage
      overlaps this proxy.
    SummonRead: A short relief answer should remove the screen and keep the lane
      from being locked.
  - TierLabel: LV2 Pressure Screen
    StageRole: Boss-side summon pressure that contests the frontline for several
      seconds and blocks player follow-up shots.
    PlayerRead: Take EN only long enough to prepare a clean response, then break
      the screen before the next boss pattern layers on top.
    SummonRead: Use SummonSlot1 or Vanguard support to absorb the curtain and reopen
      ranged punish time.
  - TierLabel: LV3 Clamp Guard
    StageRole: High-cost boss proxy that punishes overextension and demands a committed
      high-tier answer or retreat.
    PlayerRead: Back off from forward-risk lanes unless a summon answer is already
      charged.
    SummonRead: A saved LV2/LV3 summon should create a visible pressure-break window
      before counterfire.
